{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks whether the given number can be represented as sum of non-zero powers of 2 or not.\n\n    For example:\n    is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(10) == True\n    is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(5) == True\n    is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(7) == True\n    is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(11) == False\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    if n & (n - 1) == 0:  # Check if n is a power of 2\n        return True\n\n    temp = n\n    while temp > 0:\n      power_of_two = 1\n      while power_of_two * 2 <= temp:\n        power_of_two *= 2\n      temp -= power_of_two\n      if temp > 0 and (temp & (temp - 1)) != 0:\n          continue\n      elif temp == 0:\n          return True\n      elif (temp & (temp-1)) == 0:\n          return True\n    return False"}
