{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def count_tuples(tuple_list, handle_invalid='skip'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the occurrences of unique tuples in a list.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple_list: A list of tuples (or potentially other data types).\n        handle_invalid: A string specifying how to handle non-tuple elements.\n                         'skip': Non-tuple elements are ignored (default).\n                         'raise': A TypeError exception is raised.\n\n    Returns:\n        A dictionary where keys are the unique tuples, and values are their counts.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for item in tuple_list:\n        if isinstance(item, tuple):\n            if item in counts:\n                counts[item] += 1\n            else:\n                counts[item] = 1\n        else:\n            if handle_invalid == 'raise':\n                raise TypeError(\"Non-tuple element encountered: {}\".format(item))\n            # Else: handle_invalid == 'skip', so continue to the next item\n    return counts"}
