{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of possible sequences of length n where each element is a positive integer,\n    each element is greater than or equal to twice the previous element, and each element is less than or equal to m.\n\n    Args:\n        m: The upper bound for the elements in the sequence (positive integer).\n        n: The length of the sequence (positive integer).\n\n    Returns:\n        An integer representing the number of valid sequences.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    dp = [[-1 for _ in range(n + 1)] for _ in range(m + 1)]\n\n    def count_sequences_from(start_value, remaining_length, max_val, memo):\n        if remaining_length == 0:\n            return 1\n        if max_val == 0:\n            return 0\n\n        if memo[max_val][remaining_length] != -1:\n            return memo[max_val][remaining_length]\n\n        count = 0\n        for i in range(start_value, max_val + 1):\n            count += count_sequences_from(2 * i, remaining_length - 1, max_val, memo)\n\n        memo[max_val][remaining_length] = count\n        return count\n\n    total_count = 0\n    for i in range(1, m + 1):\n        total_count += count_sequences_from(2*i, n - 1, m, dp)\n\n    \n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    result = 0\n    for i in range(1, m + 1):\n        result += count_sequences(i, n, m, dp)\n    \n    return result\ndef count_sequences(start, length, max_val, dp):\n    if length == 0:\n        return 1\n    \n    if start > max_val:\n      return 0\n\n    if dp[start][length] != -1:\n        return dp[start][length]\n    \n    count = 0\n    for i in range(start*2, max_val + 1):\n        count += count_sequences(i, length - 1, max_val, dp)\n    \n    dp[start][length] = count\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/240", "solution": "def replace_list(list1, list2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Replaces the last element of the first list with the elements of the second list.\n\n    Args:\n        list1: The first list.\n        list2: The second list.\n\n    Returns:\n        The modified first list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list1:\n        return list2\n    if not list2:\n        if list1:\n            list1.pop()\n            return list1\n        else:\n            return []\n\n    list1.pop()\n    list1.extend(list2)\n    return list1"}
