{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_bitonic_subsequence_sum(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence within a given array of numbers.\n\n    Args:\n        arr (list): A list of numerical values.\n\n    Returns:\n        float or int: The maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input is not a list or if the list contains non-numerical values.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    if not isinstance(arr, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    for element in arr:\n        if not isinstance(element, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the list must be numerical.\")\n\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    iss = [0] * n\n    dss = [0] * n\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        iss[i] = arr[i]\n        dss[i] = arr[i]\n\n    max_sum = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(0, i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                iss[i] = max(iss[i], iss[j] + arr[i])\n\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                dss[i] = max(dss[i], dss[j] + arr[i])\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bitonic_sum = iss[i] + dss[i] - arr[i]\n        max_sum = max(max_sum, bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "import unittest\ndef lps(string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(string)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Base case: Single character palindromes\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the dp table in bottom-up manner\n    for cl in range(2, n + 1):  # cl is the length of substring\n        for i in range(n - cl + 1):\n            j = i + cl - 1\n            if string[i] == string[j]:\n                dp[i][j] = dp[i+1][j-1] + 2\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i][j-1], dp[i+1][j])\n\n    return dp[0][n-1]"}
