{"task_id": "Mbpp/261", "solution": "def division_elements(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise division of two tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple1: The numerator tuple.\n        tuple2: The denominator tuple.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new tuple containing the element-wise division results.\n        Returns float('inf') when dividing by zero\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If either input is not a tuple.\n        ValueError: If the tuples have different lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Input Validation\n    if not isinstance(tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(tuple2, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Inputs must be tuples.\")\n\n    # Length Check\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for a, b in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        try:\n            result.append(a / b)\n        except ZeroDivisionError:\n            result.append(float('inf'))  # Or raise ZeroDivisionError\n    return tuple(result)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/262", "solution": "def split_two_parts(input_list, L):\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list into two parts based on a specified length.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: The list to be split.\n        L: The desired length of the first part of the list.\n\n    Returns:\n        A tuple containing two lists: the first L elements of the input list,\n        and the remaining elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if L <= 0:\n        return [], input_list\n    \n    N = len(input_list)\n    \n    if L >= N:\n        return input_list, []\n    else:\n        list1 = input_list[:L]\n        list2 = input_list[L:]\n        return list1, list2"}
