{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr, n, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a contiguous subarray within a modified array\n    formed by repeating a given array k times.\n\n    Args:\n        arr (list): The input array of integers.\n        n (int): The size of the input array.\n        k (int): The number of times the array is repeated.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The maximum subarray sum in the repeated array.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    if not arr or k == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = 0\n    current_max = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_max = current_max + arr[i]\n        if current_max < 0:\n            current_max = 0\n        if max_so_far < current_max:\n            max_so_far = current_max\n\n    arr_sum = sum(arr)\n    max_wrap = 0\n    current_max = 0\n\n    for i in range(n):\n      current_max += arr[i]\n      max_wrap = max(max_wrap, current_max)\n\n    current_max = 0\n    for i in range(n-1, -1, -1):\n      current_max += arr[i]\n      max_wrap = max(max_wrap, current_max)\n    \n    max_wrap = max_wrap\n\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_so_far\n\n    if k > 1:\n        if arr_sum > 0:\n            if k > 2:\n                max_so_far = max_so_far + (k - 2) * arr_sum\n                max_so_far = max(max_so_far, max_wrap + (k-1)*arr_sum, max_wrap)\n            else:\n                max_so_far = max_wrap\n        else:\n            max_so_far = max_wrap\n\n    return max_so_far"}
