{"task_id": "Mbpp/391", "solution": "def convert_list_dictionary(list1, list2, list3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts three lists into a list of nested dictionaries.\n\n    Args:\n        list1: List of keys for the outer dictionary.\n        list2: List of keys for the inner dictionary.\n        list3: List of values for the inner dictionary.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of dictionaries.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input lists have different lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(list1) != len(list2) or len(list1) != len(list3):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input lists must have the same length.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(list1)):\n        inner_dict = {list2[i]: list3[i]}\n        outer_dict = {list1[i]: inner_dict}\n        result.append(outer_dict)\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "def get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n  \"\"\"\n  Calculates the maximum sum based on the formula:\n  f(n) = max(f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5), n)\n  using recursion and memoization.\n  \"\"\"\n  memo = {}\n\n  def calculate_max_sum(n):\n    if n == 0:\n      return 0\n    if n in memo:\n      return memo[n]\n\n    sum_of_divs = calculate_max_sum(n // 2) + calculate_max_sum(n // 3) + calculate_max_sum(n // 4) + calculate_max_sum(n // 5)\n    result = max(sum_of_divs, n)\n    memo[n] = result\n    return result\n\n  return calculate_max_sum(n)"}
