{"task_id": "Mbpp/419", "solution": "def round_and_sum(numbers):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rounds each number in a list to the nearest integer, calculates the sum of these rounded numbers,\n    and then multiplies this sum by the number of elements in the original list.\n\n    Args:\n        numbers (list): A list of numbers (integers or floats).\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The sum of the rounded numbers multiplied by the length of the original list.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input is not a list or if the list contains non-numerical values.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    rounded_sum = 0\n    for number in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(number, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in the list must be numbers.\")\n        rounded_sum += round(number)\n\n    return rounded_sum * len(numbers)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/420", "solution": "def cube_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of the cubes of the first n even natural numbers.\n\n    Args:\n        n: A positive integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        The sum of the cubes of the first n even natural numbers.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input is not an integer.\n        ValueError: If the input is not positive.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    sum_of_cubes = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        sum_of_cubes += (2 * i) ** 3\n\n    return sum_of_cubes"}
