{"task_id": "Mbpp/458", "solution": "def rectangle_area(length, width):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the area of a rectangle.\n\n    Args:\n        length (Number): The length of the rectangle.\n        width (Number): The width of the rectangle.\n\n    Returns:\n        Number: The calculated area of the rectangle. Returns 0 if either length or width is negative.\n              Raises TypeError if either length or width is non-numeric.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(length, (int, float)) or not isinstance(width, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"Length and width must be numbers (int or float).\")\n\n    if length < 0 or width < 0:\n        return 0\n\n    area = length * width\n    return area"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/459", "solution": "def remove_uppercase_substrings(input_string):\n    if input_string is None:\n        return \"\"\n\n    result = \"\"\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(input_string):\n        if 'A' <= input_string[i] <= 'Z':\n            j = i\n            while j < len(input_string) and 'A' <= input_string[j] <= 'Z':\n                j += 1\n            i = j  # Skip the uppercase substring\n        else:\n            result += input_string[i]\n            i += 1\n    return result"}
