{"task_id": "Mbpp/586", "solution": "def split_Arr(arr: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list at the nth element and adds the first part to the end.\n\n    Args:\n        arr (list): The list to split.\n        n (int): The index at which to split the list.\n\n    Returns:\n        list: A new list with the elements rearranged.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If arr is not a list or n is not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(arr, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"arr must be a list\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n must be an integer\")\n\n    length = len(arr)\n    if length == 0:\n        return []\n\n    n = n % length  # Normalize n to be within the array bounds\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return arr[:] # Return a copy of original array\n\n    return arr[n:] + arr[:n]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/588", "solution": "def big_diff(nums):\n  \"\"\"\n  Given a list length 1 or more of ints, return the difference between the largest and smallest values in the array.\n  \"\"\"\n  if not nums:  # Handle empty list\n    return 0\n  if len(nums) <= 1: #Handle list with 1 element\n      return 0\n\n  largest = max(nums)\n  smallest = min(nums)\n  return largest - smallest"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "def find_perfect_squares(lower_bound, upper_bound):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all perfect squares within a given range (inclusive).\n\n    Args:\n        lower_bound (int): The lower bound of the range.\n        upper_bound (int): The upper bound of the range.\n\n    Returns:\n        list: A list of perfect squares within the range.\n    \"\"\"\n    if lower_bound > upper_bound:\n        return []\n\n    perfect_squares = []\n    start = int(lower_bound**0.5)\n    end = int(upper_bound**0.5)\n\n    for i in range(start, end + 1):\n        square = i * i\n        if lower_bound <= square <= upper_bound:\n            perfect_squares.append(square)\n\n    return perfect_squares"}
