{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(listToSort: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of numbers in ascending order using the heap sort algorithm.\n\n    Args:\n        listToSort: The list of numbers to sort.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list containing the elements of the input list, sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(listToSort)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Build max heap\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        heapify(listToSort, n, i)\n\n    # Extract elements from heap one by one\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        listToSort[0], listToSort[i] = listToSort[i], listToSort[0]  # Move current root to end\n        heapify(listToSort, i, 0)  # call max heapify on the reduced heap\n    return listToSort"}
