{"task_id": "Mbpp/778", "solution": "def pack_consecutive_duplicates(input_list: list) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"Packs consecutive duplicates of list elements into sublists.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: The input list.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of lists, where each sublist contains consecutive duplicates.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    current_group = []\n\n    for element in input_list:\n        if not current_group or element == current_group[-1]:\n            current_group.append(element)\n        else:\n            result.append(current_group)\n            current_group = [element]\n\n    if current_group:\n        result.append(current_group)\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/780", "solution": "def find_combinations(tuple_list: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the combinations of sums from a list of tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple_list: A list of tuples, where each tuple contains two numbers.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of tuples, where each tuple represents the sum of corresponding\n        elements from all possible pairs of input tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple_list)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(tuple_list)):\n            sum1 = tuple_list[i][0] + tuple_list[j][0]\n            sum2 = tuple_list[i][1] + tuple_list[j][1]\n            new_tuple = (sum1, sum2)\n            result.append(new_tuple)\n    return result"}
